      "role": "user",
      "content": "but its not just \"deliberate manipulation\" by producers to make the video look better... what if the manipulation is more fundamental? like, what if the person in the video isn't actually the person they say they are? i've been looking at these patterns and the way the micro-expressions repeat in almost the exact same way during different interviews... it's almost like a programmed response loop. if u analyze the specific timing of those \"glitches\" across different settings, wouldnt it look more like a piece of software trying to mimic human nuance rather than just a camera error?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
